<title>UK: Virtuality up on market talk of Philips bid.</title>
<headline>Virtuality up on market talk of Philips bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK virtual reality systems and technology firm Virtuality Group Plc extended recent strong gains on Friday, fuelled by market talk of a possible takeover bid by Philips Electronics, traders said.  </p>
<p>The stock was up 1-1/2p at 76-1/2p by 1305 GMT.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Virtuality would not comment on market talk of a bid from Philips but traders seemed to be taking it seriously.</p>
<p>&quot;I've heard it from reliable sources, it seems to have been well put about,&quot; one trader said. &quot;This news has done them the world of good. They've knocked off a few sellers and should go better from here.&quot;</p>
<p>The stock fell to a low of 65p on Tuesday before being lifted by the rumours, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
